My mother looks at the screen.
"Is that your room, Maya?" she asks.
"Yes, it is my room," I answer.
"But it is a temporary room."
I lift my computer.
I show my small room to my family.
"Here is a bed," I say.
"And here is my new plant."
"It is a very nice plant," my mother says.
I turn my computer.
"And here is a window," I say.
My sister Sofía looks at my window.
"But it is very dark," she says.
"Yes, it is completely black out there," I answer.
"There is no sun in Denmark now."
It is evening, and it is cold.
"But I have my lamp," I smile.
"So it is a good room."
